B.a36=new A.fJ("1. Who this covers",'These terms are between you and ELEVO Property Management LLC ("Elevo", "we"). They cover the Elevo app and the public terms and privacy pages. They take effect on November 21, 2026. Questions go to hello@getelevo.app.')
B.a37=new A.fJ("2. Who Elevo is for","Elevo is for landlords, tenants, and vendors or contractors. It is built for residential property in Arizona, in the United States. When a landlord adds a property, the state is Arizona and the form does not let them pick another state. You must be at least 18 years old. Elevo is not for children. We do not allow anyone under 16 to use it, and we do not knowingly collect information from a child under 13. Sign-up does not ask for a date of birth.")
B.a3b=new A.fJ("3. What Elevo does, and what it does not","Elevo is software for tracking rent, repairs, documents, and messages in one place. Elevo is not a party to a lease, a sale, or a repair contract. Elevo does not employ vendors, does not run background checks on them, and does not guarantee their work. A preferred-partner listing can be reviewed before it is shown. That review is not a promise that the vendor is qualified or trustworthy. Elevo does not give legal, tax, or financial advice, including advice about Arizona eviction or lease language. The landlord More screen may show a separate real-estate contact. That person is not Elevo, and Elevo is not your broker.")
B.a3a=new A.fJ("4. Rent and deposits","Elevo does not collect, hold, or process rent or security deposits. A landlord lists the ways they prefer to be paid, such as Zelle, Venmo, a bank transfer, a check, or cash. The tenant pays the landlord directly, outside Elevo. When a tenant taps I Have Paid, and when a landlord confirms that payment, Elevo only saves a record. That record is not a payment, and it does not prove the money moved.")
B.a34=new A.fJ("5. Landlord plans","Landlords can pay Elevo for a plan. The prices on the subscription screen are: Essential, $39.99 a month or $299 a year; Unlimited, $79 a month or $699 a year; Done for You setup, $249 once; an extra property on Essential, $12.99 a month. Essential is 1 property. Each extra property is $12.99 a month. Unlimited has no property limit while the subscription is active. Tenants are not charged to use Elevo. After you confirm your email, you choose Essential or Unlimited before the landlord app opens. That choice opens Stripe and collects a card. The card is not charged that day. It is charged automatically when the 7-day trial ends unless you cancel first. After that, Stripe renews the plan until you cancel. Manage Subscription opens the Stripe billing portal, where you can change the card or cancel. When the trial date has passed and there is no paying plan, or when Stripe marks the subscription past due, canceled, unpaid, or incomplete, Elevo blocks adding another property. Everything already saved stays readable. Deleting an Elevo account turns off the login and clears the contact details. It does not remove a property, unit, or payment instruction other people still need. Deleting the account cancels the Stripe subscription immediately. There is no refund for the current period. Done for You, as the app describes it, is a one-time setup of properties, documents, tenant invitations, and a one-hour onboarding call. The app says Elevo will reach out within one business day after you pay.")
B.a3k=new A.fJ("6. Vendor plans","Vendors can pay for a listing. The monthly prices on the vendor plan screen are Basic $39.99, Featured $89.99, Preferred $149, and Platinum $199. The app does not show a yearly vendor price. Choosing a higher plan opens a Stripe checkout page and charges the new price then. Choosing a lower plan asks you to confirm, then opens the Stripe billing portal. Elevo does not change the vendor plan by itself. The screen says a downgrade waits until the end of the billing period, with no refund for unused time. Preferred and Platinum can be marked full. A full plan offers a waitlist and does not charge until a spot is confirmed.")
B.a3f=new A.fJ("7. Tenant screening","Screening uses the landlord's own RentSpree account. The landlord saves their RentSpree link in Elevo, and applicants open that link. Elevo is not part of RentSpree and is not affiliated with it. Elevo does not receive or store the RentSpree credit report. The applicant pays RentSpree, not Elevo. Elevo can store notes the landlord types, and the notes box invites a credit score or a concern. Those notes are the landlord's words, not a report from RentSpree. The landlord, not Elevo, is responsible for the Fair Credit Reporting Act and for fair housing laws, including Arizona law.")
B.a3n=new A.fJ("8. Your account","You agree to give a current name, email, and phone, and to keep your password to yourself. Elevo emails you a confirmation link, and the account is not ready until you open it. A tenant is not linked to a unit until that email is confirmed. You are responsible for what happens under your account. If you think someone else signed in, email hello@getelevo.app. Elevo does not offer two-factor sign-in. The switch in tenant settings says it is coming soon.")
B.a35=new A.fJ("9. Your responsibilities","You will follow the law that applies to you, including landlord-tenant law, fair housing law, and any license you need to do repair work. You will not use Elevo to break the law, to harass someone, or to upload a file you have no right to store.")
B.a3j=new A.fJ("10. Changes to these terms","We may update these terms. The date at the top of this page will change in the app and on the public terms page. If you keep using Elevo after that date, you agree to the update. We do not send a separate email for every wording change.")
B.a3h=new A.fJ("11. Arizona law","These terms are governed by the laws of the State of Arizona and the United States. Disputes are handled in the state or federal courts in Arizona. If you are a consumer, you may also have rights that these terms cannot take away.")
B.a3d=new A.fJ("12. Contact","Email hello@getelevo.app.")
